    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 6th prioritizing high-upside speed threats and favorable platoon splits against moderate-skill arms. **Trea Turner** (79.66) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (74.73) anchor our daily offensive floor; both benefit from advantageous matchups against left-handed and right-handed starters, respectively. **Trea Turner** is our top play, as his stolen base potential is maximized against the deliberate delivery of Springs, while **Pete Crow-Armstrong** gains a massive 14-point boost from a dynamic platoon advantage against Singer. Similarly, **Kyle Schwarber** (74.67) and **Yordan Alvarez** (66.30) remain essential pivots, with **Yordan Alvarez** providing necessary power despite the challenging matchup against Glasnow, as his elite 0.428 xwOBA effectively mitigates the SP skill penalty. **Hyeseong Kim** (63.55) earns a surprise start because he faces McCullers Jr.\u2014a starter whose delivery profile signals a high probability for a successful swipe, reinforcing our strategic underweighting of SB scarcity.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Dillon Dingler**, who fell just short of our 40-point efficiency floor at 38.75. While his 0.374 xwOBA is promising, he suffers from a heavy negative platoon split against Gray, which pushed him behind **Colt Keith** (55.38) and the rest of our active infield. We continue to monitor the status of **Christian Yelich** and **Zac Veen**, both of whom remain unavailable due to injury and minor league assignment, respectively. Meanwhile, **Kazuma Okamoto** (56.98), **Chase Meidroth** (58.07), and **Carson Benge** (59.18) are locked into the middle-to-bottom of the order; they provide reliable, if unspectacular, production, though **Carson Benge** specifically benefits from a notable park-factor boost that elevates his raw projection. With no severe weather alerts, the focus remains on leveraging these specific matchups to gain ground in the stolen base category, utilizing the aggressive baserunning profiles of **Trea Turner**, **Hyeseong Kim**, and **Caleb Durbin** to maintain our edge.",
